The merlyn@starfire.UUCP (Brian Westley) writes:
-=> Here are some things I've put into an old version of rogue; some
-=> of my earlier suggestions were put into hack by Andres, like the
-=> Wizard of Yendor.  For whoever wants to do it...

Lovely suggestions, but new objects are unlikely to be added 3.0 now;
we want to release this puppy.  Maybe 3.1.

-=> Wand of Everything: when zapped, it acts like a random wand.
-=> It will be mis-identified (if appropriate) when you first zap it.
-=> This can be very perverse.  (Don't allow wishing, though)

Sounds neat, but all wands would have to be called instead of being
identified if it were added.

-=> Wand of Lightning is only accurate for short distances; it has a
-=> chance to 'jag' every 2 or 3 segments, re:
-=>         ---
-=> @---  --
-=>     --

A bit complicated if the jag causes the bolt to bounce, but it'd make
the wands unique.

-=> Change wand of fire to fireballs: lesser effect, but an area:
-=>     \|/
-=> @----*-
-=>     /|\

Ken wanted to do something like that for spells of fireball, as
opposed to the fire breath or bolts.  If the grenade patches were
still around, they'd be useful in implementing such a thing.

-=> Poison spike trap.  When you trigger it, a number of poison spikes
-=> spring up.  You might not be able to avoid moving over them.
-=> You can fall on them, too.
-=> 
-=> ------
-=> |.^^.|
-=> |@.^^+
-=> ------

A trap trap, eh?

-=> Scroll of duplication: duplicates an item (not wishing, amulet)
-=> Can duplicate itself, but the original vanishes, so it just 'saves' it.

I wouldn't go for this; NetHack has some powerful items, 3.0 even more
of them.  It should remain hard to come by rare objects (wands of
death, for instance).

-=> Scroll of magic lamp light.  Lights a 5x5 cell instead of 3x3.
-=> This is much more useful than it sounds.

I'd like to have actual lamps work this way in 3.0.  We'll see.

-=> Ring of Weakness: If you health is > 1/2 your max, you lose 1 hp
-=> each turn.  Bad for low level characters.

I think low level characters have it tuff enuf in 3.0.

-=> Ring of wand charges: If you zap an empty wand, the ring uses
-=> up one of its zaps.  Not for wishing, obviously.

There's presently a scroll of charging in 3.0.

-=> Magic war hammer: throw it as a missile weapon and it returns, even
-=> if it hits.  A dwarf character should start with it.

That's what boomerangs are for, alto they take planning and skill to
use.  We don't have dwarf characters, altho we do have dwarf monsters,
armed with pick-axes.

-=> Chests: open them and they contain items, sometimes different, sometimes
-=> all the same type (all potions, etc).  The chest vanishes/collapses.
-=> Sometimes there are aggravated guardian monster(s) (eyes/quasits/etc)
-=> A chest of chests seems like a great find, until they open one of the
-=> chests and find more chests, and more chests,...
-=> shopkeepers don't buy them.

We have chest objects, with random objects within.  Chests may be
locked or trapped.  Chests can not be placed inside each other,
however, because that causes hairy save/restores.


